---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
import { url, whatsappLink } from '../lib/data';
const wa = whatsappLink('Hello Destiny Global Solutions, I have a privacy question.');
// Advertising text appears automatically once Google AdSense is switched on in src/config/site.ts.
const liveAsk = /^https:\/\//.test((site as unknown as { assistantApi?: string }).assistantApi ?? '');
const ads = /^ca-pub-\d{10,20}$/.test((site as unknown as { adsenseClient?: string }).adsenseClient ?? '');
---
<LegalPage title="Privacy Policy" description="How Destiny Global Solutions Limited handles personal data on the Destiny Global Opportunities website — written to match how this website actually works." updated="23 November 2026" draft={false}>
  <p>This policy explains what happens to personal information when you use the {site.platformName} website (destinyglobals.com) or contact us about our services. We have written it to match how this website actually works.</p>

  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>The website is operated by <strong>{site.companyName}</strong> (“we”, “us”), a private limited company registered in {site.registration.jurisdiction} under company number {site.registration.number}, with its registered office at {site.registration.registeredOffice}. We are the data controller for the personal information described in this policy. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>.</p>

  <h2>2. How this website is built</h2>
  <p>This is a <strong>static website</strong>. It has no user accounts, no log-in, no database and no server-side form processing. The website cannot receive or store what you type into its forms and tools. This shapes everything below.</p>

  <h2>3. Information collected automatically</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Hosting logs.</strong> Our hosting provider, Hostinger, delivers the website. Its servers process technical data such as your IP address, browser type, the pages you request and the time of each request, to deliver the site and protect it against misuse. Hostinger processes this data under its own <a href="https://www.hostinger.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Cookie-free visitor statistics.</strong> We use <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a> to count visits, see which pages are popular and which countries visitors come from. It does not use cookies or local storage, does not create a profile of you and does not track you across other websites. A small script from Cloudflare collects technical information about the page view (such as the page address, referring page, browser type, screen size and loading speed); Cloudflare processes it under its own <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a>. We use it on the basis of our legitimate interest in improving the website.</li>
    <li><strong>Google Analytics — only if you agree.</strong> When you first visit, a banner asks whether we may use Google Analytics cookies. Only if you click <em>Accept</em> do we load Google Analytics, which sets cookies (names starting with <code>_ga</code>, kept for up to 2 years) to count visits and understand how the site is used — for example which pages are visited, roughly where visitors come from (country or city) and what device and browser they use. Google receives your IP address to provide this; we have turned off advertising features and Google signals. Google Analytics is provided by Google under its own <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a>, and data may be processed in the United States. If you click <em>Reject</em>, Google Analytics is not loaded. You can change your choice at any time with “Cookie settings” at the bottom of every page.</li>
    {ads ? (
      <li><strong>Advertising (Google AdSense).</strong> We show adverts provided by Google AdSense to help fund the free information on this website. Google, as a third-party vendor, uses cookies and similar technologies to serve ads, measure them and protect against fraud. Google’s advertising cookies enable it and its partners to serve ads based on your visits to this and other websites. Visitors in the UK, the European Economic Area and Switzerland are asked for consent through Google’s consent message before personalised ads or advertising cookies are used, and can change their choice through the “Privacy and cookie settings” link that Google shows. Anyone can opt out of personalised advertising at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a> or <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">aboutads.info</a>. Learn more in <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">How Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>. We never pass names, email addresses or other information that directly identifies you to advertisers, and adverts are not endorsements by us.</li>
    ) : (
      <li><strong>No advertising.</strong> We do not use advertising networks or social media pixels.</li>
    )}
    <li><strong>Other cookies.</strong> Apart from the optional Google Analytics cookies above{ads ? ' and the advertising cookies described above' : ''}, our website does not set cookies.</li>
    <li><strong>No other third-party content on our pages.</strong> Apart from the Cloudflare statistics script{ads ? ', Google AdSense' : ''} and (only after consent) Google Analytics, our fonts, images and scripts are served from our own website. Blog photos come from the free libraries Unsplash and Pexels, but we copy them to our own website, so your browser does not contact those services. We do not embed videos, maps or social media widgets.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Information stored only on your own device</h2>
  <p>Some features save information in your browser’s <em>local storage</em>, on your own device. This information is never sent to us and we cannot see it:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>The “Ask Destiny” assistant</strong> — questions you type into the assistant are answered inside your own browser from information published on this website. They are not sent to us or to any AI service, and they are forgotten when you close or reload the page.{liveAsk && ' The only exception is the “Check live on the official website” button: if you press it, that one question (and the university website it is about) is sent to our lookup service, which runs on Cloudflare (Cloudflare Workers and Workers AI). The service reads a few public pages of that university’s own website and an AI model hosted by Cloudflare writes a short summary. We keep the answer, but not who asked, for up to 3 days so the same question can be answered again without repeating the work; your IP address is used only briefly to prevent abuse (at most 10 questions a minute). Do not include personal details in your question.'} If you choose “Talk to a person on WhatsApp”, your last question is copied to your clipboard and WhatsApp opens; nothing is sent unless you send it yourself.</li>
    <li><strong>Saved opportunities</strong> — the list of scholarships you save. You can clear it on the <a href={url('/saved/')}>Saved page</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Application planner</strong> — the applications and deadlines you add in the <a href={url('/tools/planner/')}>planner</a>. You can delete them in the planner.</li>
    <li><strong>Your cookie choice</strong> — whether you accepted or rejected Google Analytics, so we don’t ask again on every page.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Clearing your browser data also removes this information. Calendar files (.ics) you download are created inside your browser and saved to your device.</p>
  <p>Our free tools — the eligibility checker, grade converter, ECTS calculator and visa money calculator — run entirely in your browser. What you enter is not sent to us or stored.</p>

  <h2>5. Inquiry forms</h2>
  <p>Our inquiry forms check your entries in your browser and prepare a message. <strong>The website does not send or store your form data.</strong> Your information only reaches us if you choose to send the prepared message yourself:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>By email</strong> — your email app opens with the message filled in, and you press Send. Your email provider handles the message under its own terms.</li>
    <li><strong>By WhatsApp</strong> — when you choose “Copy &amp; open WhatsApp”, the message is copied to your device’s clipboard and a WhatsApp chat with us opens; you paste the message and press Send. WhatsApp is provided by Meta and handles messages under its own terms.</li>
    <li><strong>By copying</strong> — you can copy the message and send it to us any other way.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>An inquiry usually includes your name, email address, optional WhatsApp number, nationality, country of residence, education background, the scholarship or service you are interested in, and your message.</p>

  <h2>6. Contacting us directly and our social media</h2>
  <p>If you email us, message us on WhatsApp, call us, follow our WhatsApp Channel or interact with our pages on Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIn, TikTok, YouTube or Pinterest, we receive the information you share there (for example your name, number or profile and your message). Those platforms also process your data under their own privacy policies.</p>

  <h2>7. How we use your information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>to answer your questions and inquiries;</li>
    <li>to provide consultancy services you ask for, such as reviewing documents or helping you prepare an application;</li>
    <li>to keep records of our work and meet our legal, tax and accounting obligations;</li>
    <li>to correct information on our website when you report a problem.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not use your information for automated decision-making or profiling, and we do not send marketing messages unless you ask to receive them.</p>

  <h2>8. Legal bases (UK GDPR and EU GDPR)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Steps before a contract / performing a contract</strong> — when you ask about or use our services.</li>
    <li><strong>Legitimate interests</strong> — answering general questions, running and protecting our website and business, and keeping proper records.</li>
    <li><strong>Legal obligation</strong> — keeping records required by law.</li>
    <li><strong>Consent</strong> — for Google Analytics cookies, and where you choose to share information we would not otherwise need. You can withdraw consent at any time (for analytics, via “Cookie settings”).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>9. How long we keep information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Inquiries that do not lead to a service:</strong> up to 24 months after our last contact, then deleted.</li>
    <li><strong>Clients:</strong> for as long as we provide the service, then up to 6 years after it ends, to meet accounting and legal requirements and to handle any claims.</li>
    <li><strong>Copies of your documents:</strong> deleted once the service is finished, unless you ask us to keep them for a later application.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>10. Who we share information with</h2>
  <p>We do not sell personal information. We share it only:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>with universities, scholarship providers or other organisations <strong>when you instruct us to</strong> as part of a service;</li>
    <li>with service providers that help us run our business, such as our hosting, website statistics (Cloudflare and, with your consent, Google Analytics), email and messaging providers, who process it on our behalf or under their own terms;</li>
    <li>where the law requires it, or to protect our legal rights.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>11. International transfers</h2>
  <p>We work with students in many countries and have offices in the United Kingdom and Pakistan, and some of our providers operate worldwide. Your information may therefore be processed outside your own country, including outside the UK and EU. Where this happens we rely on the safeguards the law provides, such as adequacy decisions or standard contractual clauses used by our providers.</p>

  <h2>12. Security and sensitive documents</h2>
  <p>We take reasonable steps to protect the information you send us. Please do <strong>not</strong> send passwords, bank or card details through our forms, email or chat. Only send passports, transcripts or other identity documents when we have agreed with you how to share them securely. We will never ask for your passwords or for payment to “guarantee” a scholarship or visa.</p>

  <h2>13. Children</h2>
  <p>Our services are meant for adults and for students preparing for university. If you are under 18, please involve a parent or guardian before sending us your personal information. We do not knowingly collect information from children under 13.</p>

  <h2>14. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access the information we hold about you, have it corrected or deleted, restrict or object to its use, receive a copy in a portable format, and withdraw consent. To use these rights, email <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>. We will reply within one month. You can also complain to the UK Information Commissioner’s Office (<a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ico.org.uk</a>) or to the data protection authority in your country.</p>

  <h2>15. Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>Our pages link to official websites of governments, universities and scholarship providers, and to social media platforms. Those websites have their own privacy policies, and we are not responsible for them.</p>

  <h2>16. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We will update this policy when our website or services change. The date at the top shows the latest version.</p>

  <h2>17. Contact</h2>
  <p>{site.companyName}, {site.registration.registeredOffice}<br />Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>{wa && <><br />WhatsApp: <a href={wa} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">start a chat</a></>}</p>
</LegalPage>
